        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall the churadi root \"वट/वटि विभाजने\" meaning \"to divide,\" checking whether it's \"वटि विभाजने\" giving वण्टयति in the Siddhanta Kaumudi's churadi list.\n\nActually, reconsidering, if \"वट\" is written as plain अ-ending without anunāsika marking, it likely belongs to the कथादि (adanta) group alongside \"पट वट ग्रन्थे,\" so with णिच् the final अ is elided (अतो लोपः, treated sthānivat avoiding vṛddhi), yielding वटि → वटयति.\n\nFor luṅ, since the अ lopa already occurred, सन्वद्भाव is blocked (as in कथ→अचकथत्, गण→अजगणत्), so the form parallels that pattern: अववटत्, with dual अववटतम्. If instead \"वट\" were the churadi form वटँ, it would simply give वाटयति in present and a different luṅ.\n\nActually I recall this root belongs to the कथादि group within the चुरादि class (कथ, वर, गण, शठ, पट, वट, रह, स्तन...), which supports treating it as adanta and following the same pattern as कथ and गण.\n\nI'm continuing through the dhatu list, recalling more entries like ऊन, ध्वन, कूट, स्तेन, and trying to pin down whether \"वट विभाजने\" belongs here, checking against the Madhaviya dhatuvritti to confirm the adanta classification leading toward अववटतम्.\n\n",
        "signature": ""
      },
